;; video-standard.ab3 -- can a small program tell the launcher whether this machine is PAL or
;; NTSC, through its AmigaDOS return code? Compile in UAE. Not part of the game.
;; Proof for the launcher (the pal-ntsc-variants plan (git history), step 7).
;;
;; RUN 1 (2026-10-13): the detection is right in both profiles (the results files say NTSC and
;; PAL), but the script saw NTSC on both: the return code did not reach IF WARN. So the
;; answer now also goes out as a flag file, which a script reads with IF EXISTS.
;;
;; It reads NTSC (False in PAL, True in NTSC: the main project's BLITZ_CONVENTIONS note) and ends with
;;   return code 0 on an NTSC machine,
;;   return code 5 on a PAL one (5 is WARN, so a script can ask IF WARN).
;; It also creates RAM:sparky-video-pal on a PAL machine (and deletes it on an NTSC one), and writes proofs/video-standard-results.txt with what it saw and the code it meant.
;;
;; Run it in UAE in PAL mode and in NTSC mode, each time with
;;   execute sparky-dave:S/run-proof
;; and then, in the same shell:
;;   execute sparky-dave:prove-video
;; (the file prove-video at the repo root does the same, then reads the flag file).
;; The script must say PAL under the PAL profile and NTSC under the NTSC one. If the code
;; does not come through (always NTSC, or always PAL), tell me which.

WBStartup

videoIsNtsc.w = NTSC
If videoIsNtsc = True
  exitCode.l = 0
Else
  exitCode.l = 5
EndIf

If WriteFile(0, "sparky-dave:game/proofs/results/video-standard-results.txt")
  FileOutput 0
  NPrint "video-standard"
  If videoIsNtsc = True
    NPrint "this machine reports NTSC; intended return code ", exitCode
  Else
    NPrint "this machine reports PAL; intended return code ", exitCode
  EndIf
  CloseFile 0
EndIf

If videoIsNtsc = True
  If Exists("RAM:sparky-video-pal") Then KillFile "RAM:sparky-video-pal"
Else
  If WriteFile(1, "RAM:sparky-video-pal")
    FileOutput 1
    NPrint "pal"
    CloseFile 1
  EndIf
EndIf

PutReg d0, exitCode
End d0
